@page "/release-candidate"

<SeoHead Title="Product-complete candidate" Description="Review the LifeOS v27 release-candidate boundary across Desktop, Android, Website, documentation and evidence." CanonicalPath="/release-candidate" />

<main class="page-shell">
    <section class="page-intro">
        <p class="eyebrow">PRODUCT-COMPLETE CANDIDATE</p>
        <h1>One release gate across desktop, Android, web, documentation and evidence.</h1>
        <p>
            Candidate status means the planned Group 67-120 feature set is present
            for review. Public release, store submission and production-provider
            activation still require explicit owner approval.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="feature-grid">
        <article class="feature-card"><span class="status-pill">Ready</span><h2>Desktop</h2><p>Administration, review, settings, exports, evidence and communications.</p></article>
        <article class="feature-card"><span class="status-pill">Ready</span><h2>Android</h2><p>Household, work, money, communications, settings and offline state.</p></article>
        <article class="feature-card"><span class="status-pill">Ready</span><h2>Website</h2><p>Product, documentation, onboarding, releases and factual case study.</p></article>
        <article class="feature-card"><span class="status-pill">Owner review</span><h2>Release decision</h2><p>Screenshot evidence and human approval are required before any release tag.</p></article>
    </section>
</main>
